==Strategy==
This is it: after defeating all those infuriating floors, you have reached the final one. With a wide array of threatening peons backing Uril, this stage can be an extremely difficult fight. [[Surge Attack|Surges]] spawned by Uril, Devil Wife, Condemned Peng and Sinner Snache can rip through anything that isn't immune while Sir Rels, Aku Doges and Trolly Bloggers advance incessantly. You have a few ways of approaching this stage, from taking him head on with tanks or ''avoiding'' as much attacks as possible by keeping him back and using midrange attackers, similar to [[Flow Like the Stream (Merciless)|Kappy Jr's stage]].

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapstick Cats]] - A good stackable, spammable midranger that can deal with Uril and the peons effectively, though do note they are not Surge Immune and they can only survive for so long.
*[[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:N2/Idi:NX]] - Idi's immunities to surge and curse allow her to slip by and land devastating hits on Uril, greatly speeding up the battle. Idi is able to survive one Uril hit at level 34. If Uril slows her, she can recover while other units push forward. Idi's effective damage against Relics can reach a massive '''283,500''' at level 50, and when boosted by the best attack combos possible (30%) it goes up to '''368,550''' . Even with a 10% combo this value gets to '''311,850''', only around ten thousand points shy of knocking back Uril (~321,428.6) which can be easily compensated by the use of other attackers. Idi's only weakness is her low range and the obstructive peons, so sources of CC like Doron or Thunderbolt may be needed to create an opening. In her True Form, she deals enough damage for Uril to stagger in one hit at level 33 or above, although players who do have her True Form would have obviously cleared UL and hence have her at a much higher level, enabling her to potenially chain and kill Uril in just one cycle.
*[[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Awakened Doron]] - Doron is a suicide unit that fires off one attack, which causes [[Freeze]] and [[Knockback]] to Relics. His [[Immune to Curse|Curse]] and [[Immune to Surge|Surge Immunity]] combined with his massive health and 600 range [[Omni Strike]] ensure he'll almost always get the hit in, and if the Surge spawns in the right place, he can recover a lot of ground from the Relic threats. While his CC abilities and chip damage are always welcome, Doron should definitely be saved to cover other units and provide them with a window of opportunity, which can dramatically alter the outcome of the fight.
*[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]] - This stage features several peons with low range that allow Slime to fire off its devastating level 7 [[Wave Attack]], crippling oncoming threats like Sir Rel while constantly chipping Uril, although support is needed at times given Slime's foreswing isn't the fastest. It may be a risky unit to bring as if it survives, it'll serve as a stepping stone for Uril to attack.
*[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]] - Stone's extreme health and Immunity to Slow/Surge/Knockback means it'll hold the line for its brief lifetime, and works best with research combos. Although Stone never works alone, it definitely eases pressure on the stage, but it can also be a detriment by acting as a stepping stone for Uril if your units can't tank his hits.
*[[Maize Cat (Rare Cat)|Maize Cat]] - All of the threatening enemies in the stage are well within this specialist meatshield's target traits, not to mention its Curse Immunity, and its high speed allows it to keep up with the frontline. However, its vulnerabilities to Surge and [[Slow]] can still significantly impair its overall effectiveness.
*[[Ancient Egg: N003 (Special Cat)|Cat Cactus]] - A surprisingly decent pick for this stage, at level 45, it barely survives a single hit from Uril and is immune to surges, but be warned it is vulnerable to curse.
*[[Brainwashed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Mohawk Cat]] - Brainwashed Mohawk's [[Dodge Attack|Dodge]] ability targets most enemies within this stage. As much as it is inconsistent, its disposable nature and very high speed are beyond compensation.
*[[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]]/[[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Deadeye]] - With Talents, Cyberpunk's LD area attacks can slow non-Metal enemies for 4 seconds, providing valuable support by dramatically hindering Uril. Sniper is a similar story, having a shorter slow duration but with knockback to help recovering ground, and his single-slot combo benefits Doron's KB as well.
*[[Ancient Egg: N000 (Special Cat)|Ape Lord Luza]] - For players who have cleared [[Revival of Origin]] with lots of Behemoth stones, Ape Lord Luza can be a formidable force on the field. Despite its inability to outrange Uril and vulnerabilities to Aku threats here, its Massive Damage/Resistance against Relics work very well with its Curse/Surge Immunity to rain carnage at range. Ape Lord Luza however is expensive, has a long cooldown and is very slow, so finding the correct opportunity to summon it can be difficult.
*[[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Awakened Naala]] - Naala is Strong Against Relics with 100% chance to weaken them to 50%, alongside  Curse/Surge Immunity. Its far-reaching LD attacks can whittle every threat caught in their area of effect and cripple Uril's pushing power. In spite of these abilities, Naala's relatively lower damage means it is best used in conjunction with other units, preserving its health and optimizing its offense for maximum impact.
*[[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Mystic Uril/Esoteric Uril]] - Even before clearing this stage, Uril can be useful already due to his anti-Relic Slow ability and Surges to help chain Idi hits, dealing significantly more damage if the peons are already dealt with. On future replays of this stage, Uril's True Form makes things better, thanks to his newfound Strong/Curse/Slow abilities against Relic/Aku threats as well as his own Surge/Curse Immunity, not to mention his lower overall cooldown allows him to be easily replaced when lost. Much like Naala, Uril's offense isn't enough to put a dent on his own. He mostly relies on stalling the main threats for other units to catch up.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Asiluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Assassinlan Pasalan]] - Higher range, no blindspot ''and'' Area Attacks, as much as you would expect from a Cyberpunk clone in this category. Its TBA is four seconds longer than his, so if you aim to use the cheese method with these three, be sure to send this one out last. [[Long-Legged (Combo)|Its Combo]] is also a must-have in that scenario, as it increases every Cat Unit's Slow uptime by a good margin. The other participant in it, [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Leg Cat]], can provide some decent DPS support for the frontlines whenever money is plentiful.
*[[Balaluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Piccolan Pasalan]] - Good for almost all the same reasons as Assassinlan except it has freeze instead of slow. Its range however is much lower, so watch out for that.
*[[Child of Destiny Phono (Uber Rare Cat)|King of Destiny Phonoa]] - Phonoa's main highlights include its ability to outrange Uril's Omni Strike (600>550), LD which hits from 250 to potentially 1000, Surge Immunity and [[Massive Damage]] to all traited enemies. These combined factors allow Phonoa to constantly whittle everything in this stage at range and reduce them to rubble, though do beware of its vulnerability to Curse.
*[[Daybreaker Izanagi (Legend Rare Cat)|Dawnbringer Izanagi]] - Izanagi's insane damage with each hit allows him to deal a large amount of damage to Uril as well as supporting peons, especially since he is able to outrange Uril (albeit not Uril's Omni or Surge attacks). Your own Uril and Idi can be used to massively damage the enemy Uril and Izanagi can finish the job. Alternatively, Izanagi can be used in conjunction with Uril and Idi to make it easier to constantly knock back the enemy Uril. His Conjure also acts as both free damage and a way to keep enemies away, allowing your cats that outrange Uril to freely hit him.
*[[The Grateful Crane (Uber Rare Cat)|Supernova Cosmo]] - Cosmo's unparalleled range and great damage allows him to chip away at Uril's massive health pool over time, while simultaneously killing off any annoying peons with its insane wave. When supported by units like [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] or [[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Deadeye]] and basic meatshields like [[Maize Cat (Rare Cat)|Maize Cat]], talented [[Boogie Cat (Special Cat)|Gato Amigo]] or [[Ancient Egg: N003 (Special Cat)|Cat Cactus]], and [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone]], he will be nearly untouched by Uril's extreme damage. Do beware of random death surges and Cosmo speed clipping if you are using the Sniper the Cat battle item. Therefore, it is advised to turn off Sniper the Cat during Cosmo's idle animation. Overall, Cosmo is a extremely strong option for this stage
*[[Uesugi Kenshin (Uber Rare Cat)|Talented Hellrider Kenshin]] - Kenshin with her Ultra Form and anti-Relic talents proves to be a powerhouse in this stage. Her strong Anti-Relic stats and guaranteed Knockback allows her to be effective against Uril. She can sometimes even knock back Uril twice in one attack, one from the base attack and and another from her Mini-Wave. With Knockback Combos making her double knockbacks more consistent, she can even juggle Uril. Additionally, she can 3-shot Condemned Peng, knocking him back with each attack, and one-shot every other peon.
*[[Squire Luno (Uber Rare Cat)|Lunos the Luminous]] - He completely trivializes and counters this stage. Thanks to his immunities to Slow, Curse and Surge, Uril's main debuffs and attacks have absolutely no effect on him. Combined with his Resistant ability, guaranteed Knockback, Spirit with the same effect and a level 5 Mini-Surge, he can tank and make sure that Uril can't get close to your base. He can also deal with peons since they're mostly Relic/Aku, which are his target traits, his Spirit's surge can also deal with them.

